<title>BELGIUM: Cockerill falls to H1 1996 loss.</title>
<headline>Cockerill falls to H1 1996 loss.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-09-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>First-half 1996 earnings</p>
<p>(billion Belgian francs unless stated)</p>
<p>    Group net loss (ex minorities)    0.180 vs  3.107 profit</p>
<p>    Consolidated turnover	     102.6   vs 94.8</p>
<p>    Cashflow				  5.6   vs  9.4</p>
<p>NOTE - Cockerill Sambre is Belgium's largest steelmaker. It noted that first-half 1996 figures included German subsidiary Eko Stahl.  </p>
<p>Liquid steel production (in millions of tonnes)  3.2 vs 2.5</p>
<p>NOTE - Cockerill said in a statement it could not give a forecast for the full-year result given &quot;the quiet exceptional elements both negative and positive which could possibly affect events during the second half&quot;.</p>
<p>&quot;To the extent that the upward demand trend continues, 1997 should provide a more favourable economic environment for steel making,&quot; the statement said.</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
